[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186129080 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f7944f41-be32-59e2-8b16-d3d6e85a0689" "question-37f818fc-6d32-5594-93f9-04ec549a0621"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f7944f41-be32-59e2-8b16-d3d6e85a0689" :question/id #uuid "f7944f41-be32-59e2-8b16-d3d6e85a0689" :question/math-academy-id "q-85638" :question/problem "The point $P$ is located in the third quadrant and lies on the unit circle. The $y$-coordinate of $P$ is $-\\frac{3}{5}.$ What is the $x$-coordinate of $P?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the point $P$ lies on the unit circle, it must satisfy the Pythagorean theorem: \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\n$$\n\nSubstituting $y=-\\frac{3}{5}$ into the above and solving for $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(\\frac{9}{25}) & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1-\\frac{9}{25} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{16}{25} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{16}{25}} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we select the negative answer since $x$ is negative in the third quadrant. So our final answer is $x=-\\frac{4}{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6379ebf1-b8d0-5e84-b58f-943367259fab"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6379ebf1-b8d0-5e84-b58f-943367259fab" :answer-field/id #uuid "6379ebf1-b8d0-5e84-b58f-943367259fab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-84a5612c-a50c-5501-ad80-806d183376a7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-84a5612c-a50c-5501-ad80-806d183376a7" "answer-1211556a-5bf1-58e2-84e7-7950e4319711" "answer-4f32522d-6848-5f81-b69c-a543a910c74c" "answer-5eabf2f9-9a99-5893-adc9-74960dc5a0ec" "answer-15a1e317-123e-5b9f-bb99-33f0a7ca6264"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84a5612c-a50c-5501-ad80-806d183376a7" :answer/id #uuid "84a5612c-a50c-5501-ad80-806d183376a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1211556a-5bf1-58e2-84e7-7950e4319711" :answer/id #uuid "1211556a-5bf1-58e2-84e7-7950e4319711" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f32522d-6848-5f81-b69c-a543a910c74c" :answer/id #uuid "4f32522d-6848-5f81-b69c-a543a910c74c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5eabf2f9-9a99-5893-adc9-74960dc5a0ec" :answer/id #uuid "5eabf2f9-9a99-5893-adc9-74960dc5a0ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15a1e317-123e-5b9f-bb99-33f0a7ca6264" :answer/id #uuid "15a1e317-123e-5b9f-bb99-33f0a7ca6264" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-37f818fc-6d32-5594-93f9-04ec549a0621" :question/id #uuid "37f818fc-6d32-5594-93f9-04ec549a0621" :question/math-academy-id "q-124810" :question/problem "The point $P$ is located in the second quadrant and lies on the unit circle. The $y$-coordinate of $P$ is $\\frac{5}{7}.$ What is the $x$-coordinate of $P?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the point $P$ lies on the unit circle, it must satisfy the Pythagorean theorem: \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\n$$\n\nSubstituting $y=\\frac{5}{7}$ into the above and solving for $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{(\\frac{5}{7})}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(\\frac{25}{49}) & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1-\\frac{25}{49} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{24}{49} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{24}{49}} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we select the negative answer since $x$ is negative in the second quadrant. So our final answer is $x=-\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0988bf43-8be2-598d-b9b8-92f8fe65a777"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0988bf43-8be2-598d-b9b8-92f8fe65a777" :answer-field/id #uuid "0988bf43-8be2-598d-b9b8-92f8fe65a777" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-db6a37ce-de59-5b67-9bef-6c00c0d8b028" :answer-field/choices ["answer-db6a37ce-de59-5b67-9bef-6c00c0d8b028" "answer-60643ae6-c1c1-54cb-b6a5-b7b4b55166dd" "answer-2f2b35f3-d886-5c54-a151-e8d5934eab23" "answer-8bac3b6b-cbce-58bf-9b70-ee9502dfbc6f" "answer-63e5c95a-8586-50f1-b629-8de35c055a04"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db6a37ce-de59-5b67-9bef-6c00c0d8b028" :answer/id #uuid "db6a37ce-de59-5b67-9bef-6c00c0d8b028" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60643ae6-c1c1-54cb-b6a5-b7b4b55166dd" :answer/id #uuid "60643ae6-c1c1-54cb-b6a5-b7b4b55166dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f2b35f3-d886-5c54-a151-e8d5934eab23" :answer/id #uuid "2f2b35f3-d886-5c54-a151-e8d5934eab23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8bac3b6b-cbce-58bf-9b70-ee9502dfbc6f" :answer/id #uuid "8bac3b6b-cbce-58bf-9b70-ee9502dfbc6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-63e5c95a-8586-50f1-b629-8de35c055a04" :answer/id #uuid "63e5c95a-8586-50f1-b629-8de35c055a04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129081 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-336f4f03-57a6-57dc-92a1-f56dac8b2445"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-336f4f03-57a6-57dc-92a1-f56dac8b2445" :question/id #uuid "336f4f03-57a6-57dc-92a1-f56dac8b2445" :question/math-academy-id "q-124833" :question/problem "![](images/97/978383201236edb0e33057b15f0521b4547bac94a7913abba604ef1e176dc8b3.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4},$ what is the value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ?$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/8b/8b37120c20c5b9c6f07337add093d2e582d70f6f5ba2fc1b417b1ed562920173.png)\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{7}{16}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{16}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the negative answer since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta$ is negative in the second quadrant. So, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3}{4}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-23045511-0482-5a00-b7af-8abfa60c5680"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-23045511-0482-5a00-b7af-8abfa60c5680" :answer-field/id #uuid "23045511-0482-5a00-b7af-8abfa60c5680" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-60678c6c-34f6-521e-974a-d64948890b74" :answer-field/choices ["answer-47721bcb-3d8f-5a12-bcc0-33a4f7d37a4d" "answer-60678c6c-34f6-521e-974a-d64948890b74" "answer-92360fb5-afe5-5be2-afa8-7466435ca264" "answer-a8ad6c0e-f793-5edd-90c4-0ee7b8553e5b" "answer-d5e88346-21b3-5083-aad1-974d8b1176d0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47721bcb-3d8f-5a12-bcc0-33a4f7d37a4d" :answer/id #uuid "47721bcb-3d8f-5a12-bcc0-33a4f7d37a4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60678c6c-34f6-521e-974a-d64948890b74" :answer/id #uuid "60678c6c-34f6-521e-974a-d64948890b74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92360fb5-afe5-5be2-afa8-7466435ca264" :answer/id #uuid "92360fb5-afe5-5be2-afa8-7466435ca264" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8ad6c0e-f793-5edd-90c4-0ee7b8553e5b" :answer/id #uuid "a8ad6c0e-f793-5edd-90c4-0ee7b8553e5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5e88346-21b3-5083-aad1-974d8b1176d0" :answer/id #uuid "d5e88346-21b3-5083-aad1-974d8b1176d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{4}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129821 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129082 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0d53e0c0-130a-597e-9eae-4500f595f886" "question-2086b542-4ce0-5886-ad07-2a2bb6e42c3a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0d53e0c0-130a-597e-9eae-4500f595f886" :question/id #uuid "0d53e0c0-130a-597e-9eae-4500f595f886" :question/math-academy-id "q-85639" :question/problem "![](images/c2/c27074480ce1627c5f5c54596b9adaea1800bcd657a7a392c71be86b27949424.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{4}{5},$ what is the value of $\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta ?$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/57/574143239dacf6a0eb11307826c62db531384aa03b9c0f4bade4d77c66499c23.png)\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{4}{5}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{4}{5})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{16}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the negative answer since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta$ is negative in the second quadrant. So, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3}{5}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{5})}{(\\frac{4}{5})}=-\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0f7fcedc-c163-5f81-978f-4e684776d889"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0f7fcedc-c163-5f81-978f-4e684776d889" :answer-field/id #uuid "0f7fcedc-c163-5f81-978f-4e684776d889" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-87c35db5-2008-5dbd-afde-054aac1ff46a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-87c35db5-2008-5dbd-afde-054aac1ff46a" "answer-cea07d9b-f74a-524a-b08f-3e3aadb27338" "answer-89528332-60a7-50a6-aae0-62197a6a399c" "answer-d0657123-7a09-5b4d-b51a-03a6d7445550" "answer-cdd757c7-3b04-5a03-a710-bf666e048b29"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87c35db5-2008-5dbd-afde-054aac1ff46a" :answer/id #uuid "87c35db5-2008-5dbd-afde-054aac1ff46a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cea07d9b-f74a-524a-b08f-3e3aadb27338" :answer/id #uuid "cea07d9b-f74a-524a-b08f-3e3aadb27338" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{4}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89528332-60a7-50a6-aae0-62197a6a399c" :answer/id #uuid "89528332-60a7-50a6-aae0-62197a6a399c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{5}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0657123-7a09-5b4d-b51a-03a6d7445550" :answer/id #uuid "d0657123-7a09-5b4d-b51a-03a6d7445550" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cdd757c7-3b04-5a03-a710-bf666e048b29" :answer/id #uuid "cdd757c7-3b04-5a03-a710-bf666e048b29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2086b542-4ce0-5886-ad07-2a2bb6e42c3a" :question/id #uuid "2086b542-4ce0-5886-ad07-2a2bb6e42c3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-124968" :question/problem "![](images/df/df379135e9123fe9f0c3a1e03fce4898f153e321c3bd33229f3bd1c68b6249cc.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{8}{9},$ what is the value of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta ?$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/1c/1cb6ef37aaaf228273ee44de5c6fb07a59f4e6f334702b2be1425b5988705855.png)\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{8}{9}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{8}{9})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{64}{81}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{17}{81}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the negative answer since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta$ is negative in the fourth quadrant. So, $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{9}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{9})}{(\\frac{8}{9})}=-\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{8}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f8549c61-6952-565e-a79d-86243d8c0224"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f8549c61-6952-565e-a79d-86243d8c0224" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8549c61-6952-565e-a79d-86243d8c0224" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-52305d0f-2d94-5433-b04b-fbcb2e2da01d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c2449dff-2ed5-55e8-bb8a-7583e96127a0" "answer-c5dcec46-aaea-508d-b487-98620556bbc6" "answer-52305d0f-2d94-5433-b04b-fbcb2e2da01d" "answer-fd782cf0-d10b-509b-a11e-abbbc730bc24" "answer-a4770bae-6ba8-5802-bd0c-756997c15415"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2449dff-2ed5-55e8-bb8a-7583e96127a0" :answer/id #uuid "c2449dff-2ed5-55e8-bb8a-7583e96127a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{2\\sqrt{13}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5dcec46-aaea-508d-b487-98620556bbc6" :answer/id #uuid "c5dcec46-aaea-508d-b487-98620556bbc6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52305d0f-2d94-5433-b04b-fbcb2e2da01d" :answer/id #uuid "52305d0f-2d94-5433-b04b-fbcb2e2da01d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd782cf0-d10b-509b-a11e-abbbc730bc24" :answer/id #uuid "fd782cf0-d10b-509b-a11e-abbbc730bc24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4770bae-6ba8-5802-bd0c-756997c15415" :answer/id #uuid "a4770bae-6ba8-5802-bd0c-756997c15415" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186130332 :tutorial/content "For any point on the unit circle, we can draw a right triangle whose hypotenuse is the line segment between the origin and the point.\n\n![](images/b1/b1ec08957fd0d09179853d6d56c20b7058c4531bdd7e766c5b3462ba246fce2b.png)\n\nEach hypotenuse is the radius of the unit circle and consequently has a length equal to $1.$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of *any* point on the unit circle must satisfy the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\nx^2+y^2=1.\n$$\n\nWe can use this fact to find one coordinate of a point on the unit circle given the other.\n\nFor example, suppose that the $x$-coordinate of the point $A$ in the fourth quadrant on the unit circle is $\\dfrac{3}{7}.$ To find the $y$-coordinate, we substitute $x=\\dfrac{3}{7}$ into the above and solve for $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\t\tx^2+y^2&=1\\\\[5pt]\n\t          \\left(\\dfrac{3}{7}\\right)^2+y^2&=1\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac{9}{49}+y^2&=1\\\\[5pt]\n\t\ty^2&= 1-\\dfrac{9}{49}\\\\[5pt]\n\t\ty^2&= \\dfrac{40}{49}\\\\[5pt]\n\t\ty&= \\sqrt{\\dfrac{40}{49}}\\\\[5pt]\n\t        y &= \\pm \\dfrac{2\\sqrt{10}}{7}\n\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ lies in the *fourth* quadrant, $y$ must be *negative*. So we select the negative answer. Therefore, $y=-\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{10}}{7}.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186130333 :tutorial/content "By the Pythagorean theorem, we know that the equation \n\n$$\nx^2+y^2 = 1\n$$\n\nholds for any point $(x,y)$ on the unit circle. \n\nNow, we also know that for any point on the unit circle, the coordinates $(x,y)$ are related to the central angle $\\theta$ via the formulas\n\n$$\nx = \\cos\\theta, \\qquad y = \\sin\\theta.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the Pythagorean Identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2} & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last equation is called the **Pythagorean trigonometric identity**, and it holds for *every* angle $\\theta.$ This includes negative angles and angles that are larger than one full rotation." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129363 :activity/expected-seconds 840.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-f7944f41-be32-59e2-8b16-d3d6e85a0689" :question/id #uuid "f7944f41-be32-59e2-8b16-d3d6e85a0689"] ["question-f7944f41-be32-59e2-8b16-d3d6e85a0689" :question/math-academy-id "q-85638"] ["question-f7944f41-be32-59e2-8b16-d3d6e85a0689" :question/problem "The point $P$ is located in the third quadrant and lies on the unit circle. The $y$-coordinate of $P$ is $-\\frac{3}{5}.$ What is the $x$-coordinate of $P?$"] ["question-f7944f41-be32-59e2-8b16-d3d6e85a0689" :question/worked-solution "Since the point $P$ lies on the unit circle, it must satisfy the Pythagorean theorem: \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\n$$\n\nSubstituting $y=-\\frac{3}{5}$ into the above and solving for $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(\\frac{9}{25}) & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1-\\frac{9}{25} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{16}{25} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{16}{25}} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we select the negative answer since $x$ is negative in the third quadrant. So our final answer is $x=-\\frac{4}{5}.$"] ["question-f7944f41-be32-59e2-8b16-d3d6e85a0689" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-6379ebf1-b8d0-5e84-b58f-943367259fab" :answer-field/id #uuid "6379ebf1-b8d0-5e84-b58f-943367259fab"] ["answer-84a5612c-a50c-5501-ad80-806d183376a7" :answer/id #uuid "84a5612c-a50c-5501-ad80-806d183376a7"] ["answer-84a5612c-a50c-5501-ad80-806d183376a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-84a5612c-a50c-5501-ad80-806d183376a7" :answer/value "x=-\\frac{4}{5}"] ["answer-1211556a-5bf1-58e2-84e7-7950e4319711" :answer/id #uuid "1211556a-5bf1-58e2-84e7-7950e4319711"] ["answer-1211556a-5bf1-58e2-84e7-7950e4319711" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1211556a-5bf1-58e2-84e7-7950e4319711" :answer/value "x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}"] ["answer-4f32522d-6848-5f81-b69c-a543a910c74c" :answer/id #uuid "4f32522d-6848-5f81-b69c-a543a910c74c"] ["answer-4f32522d-6848-5f81-b69c-a543a910c74c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4f32522d-6848-5f81-b69c-a543a910c74c" :answer/value "x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{5}"] ["answer-5eabf2f9-9a99-5893-adc9-74960dc5a0ec" :answer/id #uuid "5eabf2f9-9a99-5893-adc9-74960dc5a0ec"] ["answer-5eabf2f9-9a99-5893-adc9-74960dc5a0ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5eabf2f9-9a99-5893-adc9-74960dc5a0ec" :answer/value "x=\\frac{4}{5}"] ["answer-15a1e317-123e-5b9f-bb99-33f0a7ca6264" :answer/id #uuid "15a1e317-123e-5b9f-bb99-33f0a7ca6264"] ["answer-15a1e317-123e-5b9f-bb99-33f0a7ca6264" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-15a1e317-123e-5b9f-bb99-33f0a7ca6264" :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{5}"] ["answer-field-6379ebf1-b8d0-5e84-b58f-943367259fab" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-6379ebf1-b8d0-5e84-b58f-943367259fab" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-6379ebf1-b8d0-5e84-b58f-943367259fab" :answer-field/correct "answer-84a5612c-a50c-5501-ad80-806d183376a7"] ["answer-field-6379ebf1-b8d0-5e84-b58f-943367259fab" :answer-field/choices "answer-84a5612c-a50c-5501-ad80-806d183376a7"] ["answer-field-6379ebf1-b8d0-5e84-b58f-943367259fab" :answer-field/choices "answer-1211556a-5bf1-58e2-84e7-7950e4319711"] ["answer-field-6379ebf1-b8d0-5e84-b58f-943367259fab" :answer-field/choices "answer-4f32522d-6848-5f81-b69c-a543a910c74c"] ["answer-field-6379ebf1-b8d0-5e84-b58f-943367259fab" :answer-field/choices "answer-5eabf2f9-9a99-5893-adc9-74960dc5a0ec"] ["answer-field-6379ebf1-b8d0-5e84-b58f-943367259fab" :answer-field/choices "answer-15a1e317-123e-5b9f-bb99-33f0a7ca6264"] ["question-f7944f41-be32-59e2-8b16-d3d6e85a0689" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-6379ebf1-b8d0-5e84-b58f-943367259fab"] [17592186129080 :knowledge-point/questions "question-f7944f41-be32-59e2-8b16-d3d6e85a0689"] ["question-37f818fc-6d32-5594-93f9-04ec549a0621" :question/id #uuid "37f818fc-6d32-5594-93f9-04ec549a0621"] ["question-37f818fc-6d32-5594-93f9-04ec549a0621" :question/math-academy-id "q-124810"] ["question-37f818fc-6d32-5594-93f9-04ec549a0621" :question/problem "The point $P$ is located in the second quadrant and lies on the unit circle. The $y$-coordinate of $P$ is $\\frac{5}{7}.$ What is the $x$-coordinate of $P?$"] ["question-37f818fc-6d32-5594-93f9-04ec549a0621" :question/worked-solution "Since the point $P$ lies on the unit circle, it must satisfy the Pythagorean theorem: \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\n$$\n\nSubstituting $y=\\frac{5}{7}$ into the above and solving for $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{(\\frac{5}{7})}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(\\frac{25}{49}) & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1-\\frac{25}{49} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{24}{49} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{24}{49}} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we select the negative answer since $x$ is negative in the second quadrant. So our final answer is $x=-\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7}.$"] ["question-37f818fc-6d32-5594-93f9-04ec549a0621" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-0988bf43-8be2-598d-b9b8-92f8fe65a777" :answer-field/id #uuid "0988bf43-8be2-598d-b9b8-92f8fe65a777"] ["answer-db6a37ce-de59-5b67-9bef-6c00c0d8b028" :answer/id #uuid "db6a37ce-de59-5b67-9bef-6c00c0d8b028"] ["answer-db6a37ce-de59-5b67-9bef-6c00c0d8b028" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-db6a37ce-de59-5b67-9bef-6c00c0d8b028" :answer/value "x=-\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7}"] ["answer-60643ae6-c1c1-54cb-b6a5-b7b4b55166dd" :answer/id #uuid "60643ae6-c1c1-54cb-b6a5-b7b4b55166dd"] ["answer-60643ae6-c1c1-54cb-b6a5-b7b4b55166dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-60643ae6-c1c1-54cb-b6a5-b7b4b55166dd" :answer/value "x=-\\frac{2}{7}"] ["answer-2f2b35f3-d886-5c54-a151-e8d5934eab23" :answer/id #uuid "2f2b35f3-d886-5c54-a151-e8d5934eab23"] ["answer-2f2b35f3-d886-5c54-a151-e8d5934eab23" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2f2b35f3-d886-5c54-a151-e8d5934eab23" :answer/value "x=-\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{5}"] ["answer-8bac3b6b-cbce-58bf-9b70-ee9502dfbc6f" :answer/id #uuid "8bac3b6b-cbce-58bf-9b70-ee9502dfbc6f"] ["answer-8bac3b6b-cbce-58bf-9b70-ee9502dfbc6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8bac3b6b-cbce-58bf-9b70-ee9502dfbc6f" :answer/value "x=\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7}"] ["answer-63e5c95a-8586-50f1-b629-8de35c055a04" :answer/id #uuid "63e5c95a-8586-50f1-b629-8de35c055a04"] ["answer-63e5c95a-8586-50f1-b629-8de35c055a04" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-63e5c95a-8586-50f1-b629-8de35c055a04" :answer/value "x=\\frac{2}{7}"] ["answer-field-0988bf43-8be2-598d-b9b8-92f8fe65a777" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-0988bf43-8be2-598d-b9b8-92f8fe65a777" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-0988bf43-8be2-598d-b9b8-92f8fe65a777" :answer-field/correct "answer-db6a37ce-de59-5b67-9bef-6c00c0d8b028"] ["answer-field-0988bf43-8be2-598d-b9b8-92f8fe65a777" :answer-field/choices "answer-db6a37ce-de59-5b67-9bef-6c00c0d8b028"] ["answer-field-0988bf43-8be2-598d-b9b8-92f8fe65a777" :answer-field/choices "answer-60643ae6-c1c1-54cb-b6a5-b7b4b55166dd"] ["answer-field-0988bf43-8be2-598d-b9b8-92f8fe65a777" :answer-field/choices "answer-2f2b35f3-d886-5c54-a151-e8d5934eab23"] ["answer-field-0988bf43-8be2-598d-b9b8-92f8fe65a777" :answer-field/choices "answer-8bac3b6b-cbce-58bf-9b70-ee9502dfbc6f"] ["answer-field-0988bf43-8be2-598d-b9b8-92f8fe65a777" :answer-field/choices "answer-63e5c95a-8586-50f1-b629-8de35c055a04"] ["question-37f818fc-6d32-5594-93f9-04ec549a0621" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-0988bf43-8be2-598d-b9b8-92f8fe65a777"] [17592186129080 :knowledge-point/questions "question-37f818fc-6d32-5594-93f9-04ec549a0621"] ["question-336f4f03-57a6-57dc-92a1-f56dac8b2445" :question/id #uuid "336f4f03-57a6-57dc-92a1-f56dac8b2445"] ["question-336f4f03-57a6-57dc-92a1-f56dac8b2445" :question/math-academy-id "q-124833"] ["question-336f4f03-57a6-57dc-92a1-f56dac8b2445" :question/problem "![](images/97/978383201236edb0e33057b15f0521b4547bac94a7913abba604ef1e176dc8b3.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4},$ what is the value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ?$"] ["question-336f4f03-57a6-57dc-92a1-f56dac8b2445" :question/worked-solution "![](images/8b/8b37120c20c5b9c6f07337add093d2e582d70f6f5ba2fc1b417b1ed562920173.png)\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{7}{16}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{16}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the negative answer since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta$ is negative in the second quadrant. So, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3}{4}.$"] ["question-336f4f03-57a6-57dc-92a1-f56dac8b2445" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-23045511-0482-5a00-b7af-8abfa60c5680" :answer-field/id #uuid "23045511-0482-5a00-b7af-8abfa60c5680"] ["answer-47721bcb-3d8f-5a12-bcc0-33a4f7d37a4d" :answer/id #uuid "47721bcb-3d8f-5a12-bcc0-33a4f7d37a4d"] ["answer-47721bcb-3d8f-5a12-bcc0-33a4f7d37a4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-47721bcb-3d8f-5a12-bcc0-33a4f7d37a4d" :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{1}{4}"] ["answer-60678c6c-34f6-521e-974a-d64948890b74" :answer/id #uuid "60678c6c-34f6-521e-974a-d64948890b74"] ["answer-60678c6c-34f6-521e-974a-d64948890b74" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-60678c6c-34f6-521e-974a-d64948890b74" :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3}{4}"] ["answer-92360fb5-afe5-5be2-afa8-7466435ca264" :answer/id #uuid "92360fb5-afe5-5be2-afa8-7466435ca264"] ["answer-92360fb5-afe5-5be2-afa8-7466435ca264" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-92360fb5-afe5-5be2-afa8-7466435ca264" :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{4}"] ["answer-a8ad6c0e-f793-5edd-90c4-0ee7b8553e5b" :answer/id #uuid "a8ad6c0e-f793-5edd-90c4-0ee7b8553e5b"] ["answer-a8ad6c0e-f793-5edd-90c4-0ee7b8553e5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a8ad6c0e-f793-5edd-90c4-0ee7b8553e5b" :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{3}{4}"] ["answer-d5e88346-21b3-5083-aad1-974d8b1176d0" :answer/id #uuid "d5e88346-21b3-5083-aad1-974d8b1176d0"] ["answer-d5e88346-21b3-5083-aad1-974d8b1176d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d5e88346-21b3-5083-aad1-974d8b1176d0" :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{4}{9}"] ["answer-field-23045511-0482-5a00-b7af-8abfa60c5680" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-23045511-0482-5a00-b7af-8abfa60c5680" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-23045511-0482-5a00-b7af-8abfa60c5680" :answer-field/correct "answer-60678c6c-34f6-521e-974a-d64948890b74"] ["answer-field-23045511-0482-5a00-b7af-8abfa60c5680" :answer-field/choices "answer-47721bcb-3d8f-5a12-bcc0-33a4f7d37a4d"] ["answer-field-23045511-0482-5a00-b7af-8abfa60c5680" :answer-field/choices "answer-60678c6c-34f6-521e-974a-d64948890b74"] ["answer-field-23045511-0482-5a00-b7af-8abfa60c5680" :answer-field/choices "answer-92360fb5-afe5-5be2-afa8-7466435ca264"] ["answer-field-23045511-0482-5a00-b7af-8abfa60c5680" :answer-field/choices "answer-a8ad6c0e-f793-5edd-90c4-0ee7b8553e5b"] ["answer-field-23045511-0482-5a00-b7af-8abfa60c5680" :answer-field/choices "answer-d5e88346-21b3-5083-aad1-974d8b1176d0"] ["question-336f4f03-57a6-57dc-92a1-f56dac8b2445" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-23045511-0482-5a00-b7af-8abfa60c5680"] [17592186129081 :knowledge-point/questions "question-336f4f03-57a6-57dc-92a1-f56dac8b2445"] [17592186129821 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["question-0d53e0c0-130a-597e-9eae-4500f595f886" :question/id #uuid "0d53e0c0-130a-597e-9eae-4500f595f886"] ["question-0d53e0c0-130a-597e-9eae-4500f595f886" :question/math-academy-id "q-85639"] ["question-0d53e0c0-130a-597e-9eae-4500f595f886" :question/problem "![](images/c2/c27074480ce1627c5f5c54596b9adaea1800bcd657a7a392c71be86b27949424.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{4}{5},$ what is the value of $\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta ?$"] ["question-0d53e0c0-130a-597e-9eae-4500f595f886" :question/worked-solution "![](images/57/574143239dacf6a0eb11307826c62db531384aa03b9c0f4bade4d77c66499c23.png)\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{4}{5}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{4}{5})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{16}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the negative answer since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta$ is negative in the second quadrant. So, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3}{5}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{5})}{(\\frac{4}{5})}=-\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$"] ["question-0d53e0c0-130a-597e-9eae-4500f595f886" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-0f7fcedc-c163-5f81-978f-4e684776d889" :answer-field/id #uuid "0f7fcedc-c163-5f81-978f-4e684776d889"] ["answer-87c35db5-2008-5dbd-afde-054aac1ff46a" :answer/id #uuid "87c35db5-2008-5dbd-afde-054aac1ff46a"] ["answer-87c35db5-2008-5dbd-afde-054aac1ff46a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-87c35db5-2008-5dbd-afde-054aac1ff46a" :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3}{4}"] ["answer-cea07d9b-f74a-524a-b08f-3e3aadb27338" :answer/id #uuid "cea07d9b-f74a-524a-b08f-3e3aadb27338"] ["answer-cea07d9b-f74a-524a-b08f-3e3aadb27338" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-cea07d9b-f74a-524a-b08f-3e3aadb27338" :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{4}{7}"] ["answer-89528332-60a7-50a6-aae0-62197a6a399c" :answer/id #uuid "89528332-60a7-50a6-aae0-62197a6a399c"] ["answer-89528332-60a7-50a6-aae0-62197a6a399c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-89528332-60a7-50a6-aae0-62197a6a399c" :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{5}{7}"] ["answer-d0657123-7a09-5b4d-b51a-03a6d7445550" :answer/id #uuid "d0657123-7a09-5b4d-b51a-03a6d7445550"] ["answer-d0657123-7a09-5b4d-b51a-03a6d7445550" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d0657123-7a09-5b4d-b51a-03a6d7445550" :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =\\frac{2}{5}"] ["answer-cdd757c7-3b04-5a03-a710-bf666e048b29" :answer/id #uuid "cdd757c7-3b04-5a03-a710-bf666e048b29"] ["answer-cdd757c7-3b04-5a03-a710-bf666e048b29" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-cdd757c7-3b04-5a03-a710-bf666e048b29" :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =\\frac{3}{5}"] ["answer-field-0f7fcedc-c163-5f81-978f-4e684776d889" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-0f7fcedc-c163-5f81-978f-4e684776d889" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-0f7fcedc-c163-5f81-978f-4e684776d889" :answer-field/correct "answer-87c35db5-2008-5dbd-afde-054aac1ff46a"] ["answer-field-0f7fcedc-c163-5f81-978f-4e684776d889" :answer-field/choices "answer-87c35db5-2008-5dbd-afde-054aac1ff46a"] ["answer-field-0f7fcedc-c163-5f81-978f-4e684776d889" :answer-field/choices "answer-cea07d9b-f74a-524a-b08f-3e3aadb27338"] ["answer-field-0f7fcedc-c163-5f81-978f-4e684776d889" :answer-field/choices "answer-89528332-60a7-50a6-aae0-62197a6a399c"] ["answer-field-0f7fcedc-c163-5f81-978f-4e684776d889" :answer-field/choices "answer-d0657123-7a09-5b4d-b51a-03a6d7445550"] ["answer-field-0f7fcedc-c163-5f81-978f-4e684776d889" :answer-field/choices "answer-cdd757c7-3b04-5a03-a710-bf666e048b29"] ["question-0d53e0c0-130a-597e-9eae-4500f595f886" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-0f7fcedc-c163-5f81-978f-4e684776d889"] [17592186129082 :knowledge-point/questions "question-0d53e0c0-130a-597e-9eae-4500f595f886"] ["question-2086b542-4ce0-5886-ad07-2a2bb6e42c3a" :question/id #uuid "2086b542-4ce0-5886-ad07-2a2bb6e42c3a"] ["question-2086b542-4ce0-5886-ad07-2a2bb6e42c3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-124968"] ["question-2086b542-4ce0-5886-ad07-2a2bb6e42c3a" :question/problem "![](images/df/df379135e9123fe9f0c3a1e03fce4898f153e321c3bd33229f3bd1c68b6249cc.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{8}{9},$ what is the value of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta ?$"] ["question-2086b542-4ce0-5886-ad07-2a2bb6e42c3a" :question/worked-solution "![](images/1c/1cb6ef37aaaf228273ee44de5c6fb07a59f4e6f334702b2be1425b5988705855.png)\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{8}{9}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{8}{9})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{64}{81}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{17}{81}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the negative answer since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta$ is negative in the fourth quadrant. So, $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{9}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{9})}{(\\frac{8}{9})}=-\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{8}.\n$$"] ["question-2086b542-4ce0-5886-ad07-2a2bb6e42c3a" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-f8549c61-6952-565e-a79d-86243d8c0224" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8549c61-6952-565e-a79d-86243d8c0224"] ["answer-c2449dff-2ed5-55e8-bb8a-7583e96127a0" :answer/id #uuid "c2449dff-2ed5-55e8-bb8a-7583e96127a0"] ["answer-c2449dff-2ed5-55e8-bb8a-7583e96127a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c2449dff-2ed5-55e8-bb8a-7583e96127a0" :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{2\\sqrt{13}}{3}"] ["answer-c5dcec46-aaea-508d-b487-98620556bbc6" :answer/id #uuid "c5dcec46-aaea-508d-b487-98620556bbc6"] ["answer-c5dcec46-aaea-508d-b487-98620556bbc6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c5dcec46-aaea-508d-b487-98620556bbc6" :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}"] ["answer-52305d0f-2d94-5433-b04b-fbcb2e2da01d" :answer/id #uuid "52305d0f-2d94-5433-b04b-fbcb2e2da01d"] ["answer-52305d0f-2d94-5433-b04b-fbcb2e2da01d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-52305d0f-2d94-5433-b04b-fbcb2e2da01d" :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{8}"] ["answer-fd782cf0-d10b-509b-a11e-abbbc730bc24" :answer/id #uuid "fd782cf0-d10b-509b-a11e-abbbc730bc24"] ["answer-fd782cf0-d10b-509b-a11e-abbbc730bc24" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fd782cf0-d10b-509b-a11e-abbbc730bc24" :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}"] ["answer-a4770bae-6ba8-5802-bd0c-756997c15415" :answer/id #uuid "a4770bae-6ba8-5802-bd0c-756997c15415"] ["answer-a4770bae-6ba8-5802-bd0c-756997c15415" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a4770bae-6ba8-5802-bd0c-756997c15415" :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{8}"] ["answer-field-f8549c61-6952-565e-a79d-86243d8c0224" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-f8549c61-6952-565e-a79d-86243d8c0224" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-f8549c61-6952-565e-a79d-86243d8c0224" :answer-field/correct "answer-52305d0f-2d94-5433-b04b-fbcb2e2da01d"] ["answer-field-f8549c61-6952-565e-a79d-86243d8c0224" :answer-field/choices "answer-c2449dff-2ed5-55e8-bb8a-7583e96127a0"] ["answer-field-f8549c61-6952-565e-a79d-86243d8c0224" :answer-field/choices "answer-c5dcec46-aaea-508d-b487-98620556bbc6"] ["answer-field-f8549c61-6952-565e-a79d-86243d8c0224" :answer-field/choices "answer-52305d0f-2d94-5433-b04b-fbcb2e2da01d"] ["answer-field-f8549c61-6952-565e-a79d-86243d8c0224" :answer-field/choices "answer-fd782cf0-d10b-509b-a11e-abbbc730bc24"] ["answer-field-f8549c61-6952-565e-a79d-86243d8c0224" :answer-field/choices "answer-a4770bae-6ba8-5802-bd0c-756997c15415"] ["question-2086b542-4ce0-5886-ad07-2a2bb6e42c3a" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-f8549c61-6952-565e-a79d-86243d8c0224"] [17592186129082 :knowledge-point/questions "question-2086b542-4ce0-5886-ad07-2a2bb6e42c3a"] [17592186130332 :tutorial/content "For any point on the unit circle, we can draw a right triangle whose hypotenuse is the line segment between the origin and the point.\n\n![](images/b1/b1ec08957fd0d09179853d6d56c20b7058c4531bdd7e766c5b3462ba246fce2b.png)\n\nEach hypotenuse is the radius of the unit circle and consequently has a length equal to $1.$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of *any* point on the unit circle must satisfy the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\nx^2+y^2=1.\n$$\n\nWe can use this fact to find one coordinate of a point on the unit circle given the other.\n\nFor example, suppose that the $x$-coordinate of the point $A$ in the fourth quadrant on the unit circle is $\\dfrac{3}{7}.$ To find the $y$-coordinate, we substitute $x=\\dfrac{3}{7}$ into the above and solve for $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\t\tx^2+y^2&=1\\\\[5pt]\n\t          \\left(\\dfrac{3}{7}\\right)^2+y^2&=1\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac{9}{49}+y^2&=1\\\\[5pt]\n\t\ty^2&= 1-\\dfrac{9}{49}\\\\[5pt]\n\t\ty^2&= \\dfrac{40}{49}\\\\[5pt]\n\t\ty&= \\sqrt{\\dfrac{40}{49}}\\\\[5pt]\n\t        y &= \\pm \\dfrac{2\\sqrt{10}}{7}\n\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ lies in the *fourth* quadrant, $y$ must be *negative*. So we select the negative answer. Therefore, $y=-\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{10}}{7}.$"] [17592186130333 :tutorial/content "By the Pythagorean theorem, we know that the equation \n\n$$\nx^2+y^2 = 1\n$$\n\nholds for any point $(x,y)$ on the unit circle. \n\nNow, we also know that for any point on the unit circle, the coordinates $(x,y)$ are related to the central angle $\\theta$ via the formulas\n\n$$\nx = \\cos\\theta, \\qquad y = \\sin\\theta.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the Pythagorean Identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2} & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last equation is called the **Pythagorean trigonometric identity**, and it holds for *every* angle $\\theta.$ This includes negative angles and angles that are larger than one full rotation."] [17592186129363 :activity/expected-seconds 840.0]] "retractions" [[17592186130332 :tutorial/content "For any point on the unit circle, we can draw a right triangle whose hypotenuse is the line segment between the origin and the point.\n\n![](images/b1/b1ec08957fd0d09179853d6d56c20b7058c4531bdd7e766c5b3462ba246fce2b.png)\n\nEach hypotenuse is the radius of the unit circle and consequently has a length equal to $1.$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of *any* point on the unit circle must satisfy the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\nx^2+y^2=1.\n$$\n\nWe can use this fact to find one coordinate of a point on the unit circle given the other.\n\nFor example, suppose that the $x$-coordinate of the point $A$ in the fourth quadrant on the unit circle is $\\dfrac{3}{7}.$ To find the $y$-coordinate, we substitute $x=\\dfrac{3}{7}$ into the above and solve for $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\tx^2+y^2&=1\\[5pt]\n\t          \\left(\\dfrac{3}{7}\\right)^2+y^2&=1\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac{9}{49}+y^2&=1\\[5pt]\n\t\ty^2&= 1-\\dfrac{9}{49}\\[5pt]\n\t\ty^2&= \\dfrac{40}{49}\\[5pt]\n\t\ty&= \\sqrt{\\dfrac{40}{49}}\\[5pt]\n\t        y &= \\pm \\dfrac{2\\sqrt{10}}{7}\n\n}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ lies in the *fourth* quadrant, $y$ must be *negative*. So we select the negative answer. Therefore, $y=-\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{10}}{7}.$"] [17592186130333 :tutorial/content "By the Pythagorean theorem, we know that the equation \n\n$$\nx^2+y^2 = 1\n$$\n\nholds for any point $(x,y)$ on the unit circle. \n\nNow, we also know that for any point on the unit circle, the coordinates $(x,y)$ are related to the central angle $\\theta$ via the formulas\n\n$$\nx = \\cos\\theta, \\qquad y = \\sin\\theta.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the Pythagorean Identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ (\\operatorname{cos}\\theta )^{2}+(\\operatorname{sin}\\theta )^{2} & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}\\theta +{sin}^{2}\\theta  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last equation is called the **Pythagorean trigonometric identity**, and it holds for *every* angle $\\theta.$ This includes negative angles and angles that are larger than one full rotation."]]}]